<title>USA: Hughes' sale draws focus on tax law - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Hughes' sale draws focus on tax law - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon Co's proposed $9.5 billion purchase of Hughes Electronics Corp's defense unit is drawing a closer eye on a tax law that lets such deals be tax-free to sellers, the Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>The growing concern should not block the deal, but it is adding pressure for congressional hearings on legislation aimed at taxing similar future deals, the story said.</p>
<p>The report also said Raytheon is designing $770 million in cost savings during the next three years from the acquisition.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
